why: Kirill on 2026-09-21 read the written block as "This still sounds confusing"; the audit called "the measured settlement scheme" plain when it is a coined modifier, and the note paraphrased an identifier into English instead of naming and placing it, so a reader gets neither the name nor an explanation; no check reaches either, since an identifier's words are the domain's words, and the Words sentence for naming an identifier with an appositive is the remedy the writer's judgement applies
labelled: 2026-09-21
--- code
export function withOnlySettlement(source: SourceConfig, scheme: Settlement): SourceConfig {
  return { ...source, settlements: [scheme] };
}
--- facts
A source offers the ledger every settlement it configures, and the preferred settlements setting only ranks them. The source returned here configures the measured settlement alone.
